+# v2-scale-depth (2026-08-22)
+
+- The MM map-share numbers in the audit (paper 49/wtr 28/land 12.5) and the
+  edge-cluster distribution (45% ring / 10% interior) are real and measurable
+  with PIL on the local refs — always re-measure MM refs yourself; the audit
+  html numbers compress them.
+- Map generator tuning is a PYTHON-PROTOTYPE-FIRST discipline: the first
+  center-suppression cut was spatially INVERTED (max() of axis distances put
+  the bias at corners, not the center) and both hunters caught it — prototype
+  with the EXACT intended formula and verify the spatial direction before
+  porting to Odin.
+- A guaranteed water ring would deterministically strand spawned nodes in the
+  sea (placement is not terrain-aware) — MM's edge read must come from a
+  STOCHASTIC bias, never a hard ring.
+- Golden re-bless for view-layer changes is T2-only: `harness run` proves T1
+  + replay byte-identical, `fold-check` proves the fold-only shift; the
+  palcheck sprite floors must be re-measured (smaller sprites → lower counts).
+- Wide-tier band must stay below the house footprint or the pipe dwarfs the
+  node it serves — check the full tier ladder after retuning standard.
