+---
+title: 'v2 scale + depth (node footprints, shadows, map board)'
+type: 'feature'
+created: '2026-08-22'
+status: 'in-progress'
+review_loop_iteration: 0
+context: []
+---
+
+<frozen-after-approval reason="human-owned intent — do not modify unless human renegotiates">
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** Our nodes are too big relative to the network (house 36px vs MM ~0.5–1.0× road), shadows are a uniform blob under every node (MM scales them per building), and the background map is water-dominant (49% water vs MM's 26% paper-dominant board).
+
+**Approach:** Shrink node footprints toward MM's ratios, make shadows per-footprint (size-scaled ink + down-right offset), and rebalance the procedural map to a paper-dominant board with warm land tint and edge-clustered water. View-layer constants + palette tokens only.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- View-layer constants + palette tokens only: `app/render/sprites.odin` (sprite targets, sprite_shadow), `app/render/view.odin` (tier_pipe_width, draw_building), `app/render/map.odin` (generator constants), `data/palette.json` + `app/render/palette.odin` (new `land` token only — no existing token edited).
+- No geometry/sim changes, no LOG_VERSION bump, no catalog (data/balance.json etc.) edits — cat.hash is golden-poison.
+- Deliberate golden re-bless: cause-documented per capture (node size + shadows + map share). T1 hashes must stay byte-identical (view-layer only — verify with `harness run` T1 legs + fold-check).
+- Palette JSON additions only: existing keys byte-identical, re-emit in the original aligned format (the node-clarity trap: json.dump reformats — keep minimal diff).
+- Measure MM refs with Python; never copy MM bytes into the repo.
+- After scaling, re-check the 427×240 thumbnail read — smaller nodes must NOT lose the network hero read (coordinate with v2-network-pop, already merged in base).
+
+**Ask First:** (none — the briefing pre-approves the scale/shadow/map targets; values chosen within the briefing's stated ranges)
+
+**Never:**
+- No sprite art regeneration (the Blender silhouette job is separate — this job only scales what exists).
+- No atmospheric haze / far-node blur (DIRECTION.md §5 is the separate N2/N3 harmony job).
+- No UI panel/forecast/health-meter changes.
+- No changes to the a11y mode tables (they override the signal set; the new `land` token is NOT a remappable token — like canvas, it is not in the remap set).
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Terminal sprite draw | any role, sprites loaded | footprint per new role target (house 0.9, sbiz 1.1, host 1.15, campus 1.4 tiles) | fallback primitive path unchanged (only reachable with missing assets) |
+| Router puck draw | any port tier | puck target scales by the tier bbox ratio around the new base (1.30 → 1.15 tiles) | degenerate bbox guard unchanged (sprite_blit_dst ok=false) |
+| Shadow draw | any node | per-footprint ellipse: house 0.5w×0.3h / campus 0.7w×0.4h, ink 12–18% by size, offset down-right ~2px | rlsw ellipse fill alpha-blends (the 7.1 field note — fills are safe, lines are not) |
+| Map generation | seed 7 world 1040×780 | paper-dominant: world water ~33%, land ~50%, park ~12.5% with an edge water bias (border ~45% water vs interior ~30% — MM edge-clustered) | map_cells_hash pin re-blessed; same-seed stability + seed-sensitivity legs must still pass |
+| Map frame | 1280×720 fit | margins render canvas (paper), not water — water share drops from 51% to ~26% of the frame | grid lines clip to the world rect (they currently run across the full window) |
+| A11y oracle | all three CVD modes | water/park/coast vs the new land tint must separate ≥40 (the oracle pair list uses canvas as the land reference — must switch to the land token) | if a pair fails, tune the land tint within the warm-cream family until green |
+| Palette parse | missing/broken JSON | fallback_palette gains the land token default | same tolerant parse as today |
+
+</frozen-after-approval>
+
+## Code Map
+
+- `app/render/sprites.odin` -- sprite target procs (house/host/sbiz/campus/puck) + `sprite_shadow` (the per-footprint shadow) + `sprite_blit` (threads the shadow spec)
+- `app/render/view.odin` -- `draw_building` (picks per-role shadow spec + target), `tier_pipe_width` (band widths: standard 5.5 → 7.4 world px → 15px band at fit), `map_draw` (frame fill → canvas, grid clip to world rect)
+- `app/render/map.odin` -- `MAP_LAND_LEVEL`/`MAP_PARK_LEVEL`/new edge-ring + center-suppress constants; `map_color` Land → new land token
+- `app/render/palette.odin` + `data/palette.json` -- ADD `land` token (warm cream, ~(237, 226, 200) canvas + slight warm shift)
+- `harness/palcheck.odin` -- map-token pins (land color, water share, park share), a11y map pairs canvas→land, MAP_IDENTITY_PIN re-bless
+- `tools/derive_a11y_palettes.py` -- the map-pair reference (water/park/coast vs land) must mirror the oracle
+
+## Tasks & Acceptance
+
+**Execution:**
+- [ ] `app/render/sprites.odin` -- retune `sprite_house_target` 1.50→0.9, `sprite_small_biz_target` 1.60→1.1, `sprite_host_target` 1.75→1.15, `sprite_campus_target` 2.20→1.4, `sprite_puck_target` 1.30→1.15; add a per-role Shadow_Spec (rx/ry fractions + ink alpha) threaded through `sprite_blit`; offset down-right ~2px fixed (not scaled)
+- [ ] `app/render/view.odin` -- `tier_pipe_width`: narrow 3.5→4.7, standard 5.5→7.4 (band 11.2→15px at fit), wide 8.5→11.4 (proportional); `map_draw` frame fill water→canvas + grid clipped to the world rect; `draw_building` passes the role's shadow spec
+- [ ] `app/render/map.odin` -- generator: guaranteed water ring at the world border (~1 tile), interior land level lowered toward center (edge-clustered water like MM), MAP_PARK_LEVEL retuned so parks stay accent (~8–10% frame); `map_color` Land → palette.land
+- [ ] `app/render/palette.odin` + `data/palette.json` -- add `land` token (warm cream; ADDITIONS ONLY, no existing token edited); parse + fallback + Palette struct field
+- [ ] `harness/palcheck.odin` -- a11y pair list: water/park/coast vs `p.land` (replacing canvas as the land reference); map-token pins re-measured from the re-blessed goldens; MAP_IDENTITY_PIN re-blessed; sprite pin floors re-measured (smaller nodes → fewer pixels of each canon tone — re-pin with measured floors)
+- [ ] `tools/derive_a11y_palettes.py` -- map-pair section: land reference = the new land token (derivation record must match the oracle)
+- [ ] Re-bless all affected goldens (`harness save`) + T1 verification (`harness run` all 46 green + T1 hashes unchanged + fold-check) + `harness palcheck` green
+- [ ] Thumbnail gate: render a fit capture, downscale to 427×240, verify the network hero read survives smaller nodes (pixel-scan: pipe band ≥ ~5px at 427×240, node ≥ ~4px)
+
+**Acceptance Criteria:**
+- Given the fit view (1280×720), when nodes render, then house ≈ 21.6px and campus ≈ 33.6px footprints (0.9 / 1.4 tiles × 26px × 12/13 scale), i.e. house:band ≈ 1.44× (down from 3.2×), campus:band ≈ 2.24× (down from 4.7×) — before/after numbers in the PR body.
+- Given any node, when its shadow draws, then the ellipse scales with the footprint (house 0.5w×0.3h → campus 0.7w×0.4h) with ink 12–18% by size and a fixed ~2px down-right offset.
+- Given the standard tier, when a pipe band renders, then the band is ~15px at fit (tier_pipe_width 7.4 × 2.2 × 12/13), up from 11.2px.
+- Given a map frame, when the world renders, then frame water share drops from ~49–51% to ~26–28% (margins canvas + edge-clustered world water) and parks stay an accent (~8–10%), measured from the re-blessed juice golden; numbers in the PR body.
+- Given the re-blessed goldens, when `harness run` + `harness palcheck` execute, then all 46 demos green with T1 hashes byte-identical to the pre-change blessing and palcheck green (including the a11y oracle with the land token as the map reference).
+- Given the 427×240 thumbnail of a fit capture, when downscaled, then the network (pipes + nodes) still reads as the hero element.
+
+## Design Notes
+
+**Scale math (fit view):** world 40×30 tiles × 26px, fit into 1280×720 → scale = 12/13. Current house = 1.50 × 26 × 12/13 = 36px (3.2× the 11.2px standard band) → target 0.9 tiles = 21.6px (1.44× the 15px band). Campus 2.2 → 1.4 tiles = 33.6px (2.24× band — MM large blocks are 1.0–2.7× road width). Puck base 1.30 → 1.15 tiles; tier ladder (bbox ratio × 1.15/1.30) preserved.
+
+**Shadow:** current = uniform 0.64w×0.36w ellipse @ 40/255 ink (16%), offset +0.06w/+0.12w. Target per MM image_07: ellipse radii as fractions of the DRAWN footprint (rx house 0.5×w, campus 0.7×w; ry ~0.3×h house → 0.4×h campus — the same radii convention the old 0.64w/0.36w used; the full ellipse is 2× the fraction), ink alpha 12–18% by footprint size, fixed offset (2,3)px down-right. Shadow color stays the ink tone {51,65,79}.
+
+**Map:** MM image_01 measured: 49% paper / 28% water / 12.5% warm-land+green, water edge-clustered (45% at the outer ring vs 10% interior). Ours: 51% frame water (margins are water!), 35% canvas, 9.5% park, water uniformly scattered. Fix: (a) frame fill water→canvas (margins become paper — the single biggest lever: −25% frame water); (b) EDGE WATER BIAS — the land threshold rises toward the nearest border (min() of the axis distances — the r1 max() bug put the bias only at corners) so coastlines hug the board edge and the interior stays drier (world water ~33%, border ~45% vs interior ~30%); water stays STOCHASTIC everywhere — placement is not terrain-aware, and a guaranteed ring would strand border spawns in the sea (the r1 review finding); (c) parks trimmed to accent; (d) `land` token = warm golden cream (239,228,186) — visibly distinct from the paper canvas (sRGB distance ~14 vs the first cut's ~7), a11y-verified: worst CVD distance 52.8 (deutan coast) vs the 40 floor.
+
+**A11y ripple:** the oracle's map pairs are `water/park/coast vs canvas` — with a distinct land token, they must compare against `p.land` (the actual landmass color). The threshold membership test now checks BOTH ends of each pair (r1: pr[0]-only keying silently escalated reversed pairs to 48). Candidate land tints were verified numerically against the SHIPPED mode tables (worst-case 52.8 deutan-coast / 55.1 tritan-park — passes 40 with margin).
+
+**Golden re-bless discipline:** T1 hashes + .log.bin are view-layer-immune (no sim change) — the re-bless is T2-PNG-only + palcheck pins (map identity pin, sprite tone floors re-measured on the smaller sprites). Use fold-check to prove the shift is render-only.
+
+## Verification
+
+**Commands:**
+- `./bin/harness run` -- all 46 demos green; T1 hashes byte-identical to the pre-change blessing (the run compares them)
+- `./bin/harness save` -- deliberate re-bless of the affected T2 goldens, then `./bin/harness run` green again
+- `./bin/harness fold-check <prev-catalog-hash> <prev-tick1>` -- proves a fold-only shift (render-only)
+- `./bin/harness palcheck` -- all checks green incl. the a11y oracle + map pins
+- `tools/ci-local.sh --mac` -- all 10 gates green natively
+- `python3 tools/blur_gate.py` -- node-type blur separation still ≥15° after the scale change (the shrunk sprites must not lose the clarity win)
+
+**Manual checks (if no CLI):**
+- 427×240 thumbnail downscale of a re-blessed juice capture — the network read must survive.
