+# v2 scale + depth: node footprints, per-building shadows, paper-dominant map
+
+Closes the user's in-review feedback (2026-08-22): "the houses are smaller in
+MM vs PP... They used shadows to create depth. Houses have smaller shadows and
+the buildings have larger shadows... compare the background maps as well."
+
+All changes are **view-layer constants + palette tokens only** — no geometry,
+no sim, no LOG_VERSION. T1 hashes and `.log.bin` byte-identical (fold-check
+PASS); the golden re-bless is T2-PNG-only and cause-documented below.
+
+## What changed
+
+### 1. Node scale (MM 0.5–1.0× road ratio) — `app/render/sprites.odin`
+
+| Role | Before | After | Footprint @fit | :band ratio |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| house | 1.50 tiles | 0.90 | 36px → 21.6px | 3.21× → **1.44×** |
+| small_biz | 1.60 | 1.10 | 26.4px | 1.76× |
+| host | 1.75 | 1.15 | 27.6px | 1.84× |
+| campus | 2.20 | 1.40 | 52.8px → 33.6px | 4.73× → **2.24×** |
+| router puck | 1.30 | 1.15 | 31.2px → 27.6px | (the direction doc's 27px puck) |
+
+`tier_pipe_width` (`app/render/view.odin`): narrow 4.5 / standard 7.4 / wide
+10.5 world px → the standard band goes **11.2px → 15.0px at fit** (house:band
+3.2× → 1.44×, within the briefing's 1–2× acceptance). The wide tier is capped
+so a pipe never dwarfs the node it serves (wide band 21.3px < house 21.6px —
+r1 review finding).
+
+### 2. Per-footprint shadows — `app/render/sprites.odin`
+
+The uniform 0.64w×0.36w / 16%-ink blob under every node is replaced by a
+per-role `Shadow_Spec` (radii as fractions of the drawn footprint, the same
+convention the old constants used):
+
+| Role | rx | ry | ink |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| house | 0.50w | 0.30h | 12% (31) |
+| small_biz | 0.55w | 0.33h | 13% (33) |
+| host | 0.60w | 0.35h | 14% (36) |
+| campus | 0.70w | 0.40h | 18% (46) |
+| puck | 0.60w | 0.35h | 14% (36) |
+
+Offset is a **fixed (2,3)px down-right** (MM's constant light-direction cue,
+not a scaled offset). Small houses get small tight shadows; big blocks get
+larger ones (MM image_07 read).
+
+### 3. Paper-dominant map board — `app/render/map.odin` + `view.odin` + palette
+
+Measured against MM image_01 (49% paper / 28% water / 12.5% warm land+green):
+
+| Frame share | Before | After | MM |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| water | 49.0% | **26.1%** | 26% |
+| paper + land | 34.1% | **59.0%** | 51+11 = 62% |
+| park | 9.4% | 7.5% | ~9–11% |
+
+Three levers:
+- **Frame fill water → canvas** (`view.odin map_draw`): the camera-fit margins
+  were water — a quarter of the frame. They are now the paper board, and the
+  grid clips to the world rect (clean margins, MM's whitespace read).
+- **Edge water bias** (`map.odin`): the land threshold rises toward the
+  nearest border (min() of the axis distances, sharpened by repeated squaring
+  — no libm), so coastlines hug the board edge and the interior stays drier:
+  border water ~44% vs interior ~30% (MM 45/10; the interior floor is higher
+  because placement is not terrain-aware and the play surface needs lakes
+  within reach). Water stays **stochastic everywhere** — no guaranteed sea
+  ring, so spawned nodes never deterministically sit in water (r1 finding).
+- **`land` token added** (`data/palette.json` + `palette.odin`, ADDITIONS
+  ONLY): the warm golden-cream landmass `[239, 228, 186]` — visibly distinct
+  from the paper canvas (sRGB distance ~14), verified ≥40 CVD distance from
+  water/park/coast under all three shipped mode tables (worst 52.8,
+  deutan-coast). Parks re-tuned (park level 0.72 → 0.76) to accent.
+
+## Goldens re-blessed (deliberate, cause-documented)
+
+The re-bless is **T2-PNG-only**: `harness run` T1 hashes + replay byte-
+identical (view-layer change), `fold-check` PASS (the tick-1 shift is the
+catalog fold alone). All 46 demos re-saved; every capture carries the node
+footprint + shadow + map changes. Palcheck pins re-measured on the re-blessed
+frames (map water/land/paper/park/coast floors, MAP_IDENTITY_PIN, the B1
+sprite canary floors — smaller sprites, floors re-pinned with margin).
+
+## Verification
+
+- `tools/ci-local.sh` (linux container) — **10/10 gates green**
+- `tools/ci-local.sh --mac` — 10/10 green (one transient odin segfault on the
+  PP_DEBUG build in the first run; standalone + re-run green)
+- `harness palcheck` — all green incl. the a11y oracle with the land token as
+  the map reference (the pair-membership test now checks both ends)
+- `blur_gate.py` — GATE GREEN (all node-type pairs ≥15°, saturation band
+  0.271) — the shrunk sprites keep the node-clarity win
+- Thumbnail gate: network-hero pixel share at 427×240 unchanged (3.31% →
+  3.30%); standard band 5.0px, house 7.2px at thumbnail — the network still
+  reads as the hero
+- 46/46 goldens green; fold-check PASS
+
+## Decisions & rationale
+
+- **house:band 1.44× vs MM's 0.5–1.0×**: the briefing's acceptance explicitly
+  targets 1–2× (MM's road is ~2px at board scale — ours must stay legible on
+  the 427×240 thumbnail); 1.44× is the briefing's own bar, measured.
+- **Land tint is a golden cream, not a deeper tan**: a deeper warm tint
+  collides with the coast token under CVD (measured: deutan 35 < 40) — the
+  oracle's coast pair is the binding constraint. The chosen tint keeps the
+  warm landmass visibly distinct from paper for normal vision while passing
+  all three CVD simulations with margin. The a11y mode tables were NOT
+  re-derived: the land pairs pass the shipped tables (52.8 worst) — a
+  re-derivation would churn the tables without changing the outcome.
+- **Edge bias instead of a guaranteed water ring**: placement is not
+  terrain-aware (v1), so a guaranteed ring would deterministically strand
+  border spawns in the sea. The bias keeps MM's edge-clustered read while
+  keeping water stochastic.
+- **Shadow fractions are radii** (full ellipse = 2× the fraction), matching
+  the old code's convention — house full 1.0w×0.6h is tighter than the old
+  1.28w×0.72w blob, campus 1.4w×0.8h is larger.
+- **Wide tier capped at 10.5** (band 21.3px < house 21.6px) so no pipe ever
+  visually dominates the node it serves; the standard tier carries the
+  briefing's 15px target.
+- **Placement not terrain-aware remains a known limitation** (pre-existing,
+  out of scope — no sim changes in this job).
+
+Evidence: `_bmad-output/scale-depth-evidence/` (frame before/after, node
+crops, thumbnail before/after) — regenerated from the re-blessed goldens.
